{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And he said to the wicked one, etc.</b> Meaning, to the wicked one who was among them. And his saying <b>your fellow</b> — even if he were indeed wicked like you, why should he swallow up a righteous man from him? Or it may intend that he perceived that one was wicked and one was blameless who had not wronged him; therefore he said to the wicked one: why do you strike a man who has incurred no obligation to you and did not seek your harm — and this is what he meant by <b>your fellow.</b> And even though it says at first שני אנשים נצים (two men struggling), it may be found that one was contending without cause, on account of his wickedness, and the other was contending over his own cause unjustly."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:30.109986388Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}